      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dranesville takes its name from Washington Drane, a settler who arrived in 1810.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dranesville%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Washington Drane opened Drane’s Tavern, a hotel‑store‑saloon at the crossroads, which still stands on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dranesville%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1850s railroad from Alexandria to Leesburg, followed by cars, slowly faded Dranesville’s importance.",
